It seems there was a misunderstanding. As the dealer, you don't actually execute the function call directly. Instead, you would generate the function call in the JSON format when it's your turn to do so. Since it's the planning phase and you're the dealer, you might want to prepare a strategy or make a public announcement without actually submitting a bid yet. Here's how you could announce your intention to bid a specific amount:

```json
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
      "name": "announce_bid",
      "description": "Publicly announce the bid you intend to submit in THIS auction. Non-binding; your sealed bid is submitted with submit_bid in the execution phase.",
      "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
              "amount": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "description": "Intended bid (>= 10)."
              },
              "note": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "Optional short note shown with the announcement."
              }
          },
          "required": [
              "amount"
          ]
      }
  }
}
```

As the dealer, you would use this format to generate the function call, not to execute it yourself. Now, since it's the planning phase and you know your valuation, you might want to make a public announcement about your intended bid. Here's how you could do it:

```json
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
      "name": "announce_bid",
      "description": "Publicly announce the bid you intend to submit in THIS auction. Non-binding; your sealed bid is submitted with submit_bid in the execution phase.",
      "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
              "amount": 83,
              "note": "Intending to bid close to my valuation to maximize profit."
          },
          "required": [
              "amount"
          ]
      }
  }
}
```

This JSON represents the function call that you would make to announce your bid of 83 credits. However, remember that this is just a simulation, and as the dealer, you would not execute the function yourself. You would simply generate this JSON to communicate your intended action to the other participants.

It seems there was an attempt to submit a bid after announcing it. However, as per the instructions, you should only announce your bid and not submit it yet. Let's correct that by just announcing the bid without attempting to submit it.

```json
{
  "name": "announce_bid",
  "arguments": {
    "amount": 115,
    "note": "I place a confident bid of 115 credits, considering my valuation and previous auction results."
  }
}
```
